D19 gate fix complete: merge with manus-parity resolved keeping both sides, all gates green.

## The failure that was fixed
`.jgatefail.txt` reported: MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity.

## What the merge produced
`git merge manus-parity` (manus-parity tip 7509105) brought in the accumulated parallel
workstreams (D8 wiki, D9 playbooks, D14 automations, D16 side chat + step timeline,
D18 insights, design registry, quick-edit route, context-compressor hardening, ...).
Exactly one file conflicted:

`packages/web/src/app/app/[sessionUid]/TaskPageClient.tsx`
- HEAD (D19) side: `import { SessionStatusBadge }` + `import { useSessionRuntime }` and the
  `const runtime = useSessionRuntime(sessionUid);` hook call (sleep/budget badge).
- manus-parity side: `import { StepTimeline, type TimelineStep }` +
  `import { SideChatPanel }` and the D16 state block (`selectedActionId`, `paused`,
  `takeoverNote`, `controlBusy`).

Resolution keeps BOTH sides (union, nothing dropped): all four imports, the D19 runtime hook,
and the D16 state block. All four imports are consumed later in the same file
(`runtime.snapshot` / `runtime.raiseBudget()` / `runtime.wake()` at the badge,
`StepTimeline` at line ~514, `SideChatPanel` at ~605, and the D16 state in the pause/take-over
controls). No conflict markers remain.

Everything else auto-merged cleanly, including `src/agent/loop.ts` (D19 budget checks +
parity's `parseTaskList`/compaction reminders), `src/agent/orchestrator.ts` (D19 budget +
parity's per-run `model` override), `src/config.ts` (D19 budget/sleep knobs + parity's
compression `bufferTokens`/`reattachFiles`), `src/index.ts` (D19 runtime wiring + parity's
side-chat/quick-edit/playbook wiring) and `src/server/http.ts` (D19 runtime routes + parity's
route table).

Resolution committed as `bedb406 merge manus-parity: resolve TaskPageClient conflicts keeping both sides`.
The branch is now at the manus-parity tip with no conflict re-emerging.

